# Command fnm

## What does this command do:

Fast Node Manager — install, switch, and manage multiple Node.js versions. Uses `.node-version` or `.nvmrc` files for per-project version pinning.

## Installed from

For Fedora install using:
```
curl -fsSL https://fnm.vercel.app/install | bash
# or download the binary directly:
curl -fsSL https://github.com/Schniz/fnm/releases/latest/download/fnm-linux.zip \
  -o /tmp/fnm.zip && unzip /tmp/fnm.zip -d ~/.local/bin && chmod +x ~/.local/bin/fnm
```
Then add shell integration to ~/.bashrc or ~/.zshrc:
```
eval "$(fnm env --use-on-cd)"
```

## Command path

For Fedora run: ~/.local/bin/fnm  (FNM_DIR defaults to ~/.local/share/fnm)

## Command documentation

Docs can be found at https://github.com/Schniz/fnm

## Command options

# Show installed version
fnm --version

# --- Installing Node versions ---

# Install latest LTS
fnm install --lts

# Install a specific version
fnm install 22
fnm install 22.14.0

# Install latest available
fnm install latest

# --- Using a version ---

# Switch to a version in the current shell
fnm use 22
fnm use lts/iron

# Switch based on .nvmrc or .node-version in current dir
fnm use

# --- Listing ---

# List locally installed versions
fnm list
fnm ls

# List all available remote versions
fnm list-remote
fnm ls-remote

# List LTS versions only
fnm list-remote --lts

# Show current active version
fnm current

# --- Default version ---

# Get the current default
fnm default

# Set a version as default (used in new shells)
fnm default 22

# --- Aliases ---

# Create a named alias
fnm alias 22.14.0 work-project

# Remove an alias
fnm unalias work-project

# --- Uninstalling ---

fnm uninstall 20
fnm uni 20

# --- Project version pinning ---

# Create a .node-version file (fnm and volta compatible)
node --version > .node-version

# Create a .nvmrc file (nvm compatible)
node --version > .nvmrc
# fnm reads both formats; .node-version takes precedence

# With --use-on-cd in shell init, fnm switches automatically on cd

# --- Environment ---

# Print env vars (used in shell init)
fnm env
fnm env --use-on-cd        # also hooks cd to auto-switch

# Run a command in a specific Node context without switching shell
fnm exec --using 20 node --version

# --- Shell completions ---

fnm completions --shell bash >> ~/.bash_completion
fnm completions --shell zsh  >> ~/.zshrc
fnm completions --shell fish > ~/.config/fish/completions/fnm.fish
